* wiz1up - WizCon1: single-connection passthrough server with a login on the raw /wz.
* Needs: wizi, wizcon (module on the network). Nothing else running on /wz.
* Tear down with wiz1down.
echo * WizCon1 - single passthrough connection with a login on /wz (raw path)
echo * Needs: wizi already run (iniz /wz + modem /wz) and the module on the network (wizcon)
xmode /wz eko=0
echo AT+CIPSTATUS>/wz
modem /wz
echo ATE0>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPSTA_CUR?>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPSERVERMAXCONN=1>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPMUX=1>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPMODE=1>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPSERVER=1,23>/wz
modem /wz
echo AT+CIPSTO=0>/wz
modem /wz
echo * Server up. From the remote client connect to port 23 of the IP shown above...
* -t0 waits for the module's next line: the client's 0,CONNECT. On this raw
* path that wait is needed, because AT+CIPSEND (enter passthrough) must be
* sent only after the connection exists.
modem -t0 /wz
echo AT+CIPSEND>/wz
modem /wz
xmode /wz eko=1
tsmon /wz&
echo * Passthrough login running on /wz - ONE client at a time.
echo * Do not run wiz4up, wiz1stat or read /wz from the console while it is up.
